{
  "about": "Payment outcomes signed by the payer (docs/adr/0006-payer-signed-outcomes.md). Generated by scripts/check-outcome-vectors.mjs: do not edit by hand. Each key is keccak256(\"sigvara/payment-outcome/vector/<name>\") and none is stored. A case is valid when OpenZeppelin 5.6.1's SignatureChecker accepts its signature for its payer over its digest, which is always under `domain`. An account of kind owner, longer, short or writes answers ERC-1271 as test/PaymentOutcome.t.sol's accounts do. The cases that need a payment, a clock or state held by an oracle (a second signature, a negative under `positive`, import from a peer, an owner rotating between acceptance and import) are tested end to end in oracle/payer-outcome.test.js.",
